      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "*See also #45800 and #45801.*\r\n\r\n**Godot version:** 3.2.4rc1\r\n\r\n**OS/device including version:** Fedora 33, Firefox 85\r\n\r\n**Issue description:**\r\n\r\nUnlike the native version of Godot, in the web editor, pressing F8 while focusing on the Game tab DOM canvas won't stop the running project.\r\n\r\n**Steps to reproduce:**\r\n\r\n- Start the web editor (or even the project manager).\r\n- Run the project by pressing <kbd>F5</kbd> while the editor frame is focused.\r\n- The editor will switch to the Game tab. Press <kbd>F8</kbd> (before or after clicking on the game's frame). Nothing happens.\r\n\r\nIn the native version of Godot, the project will stop when you press <kbd>F8</kbd> while the window is focused.\r\n\r\n**Minimal reproduction project:** N/A",
