      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "**Godot 3.2.1**\r\n\r\n\r\n**Windows 10, Intel HD 4000 Chipset**\r\n\r\n\r\nI'm using a mirrored texture and its region to scroll it along its Y axis infinitely. The problem comes when trying to rotate the scrolling texture. It seems that its pivot point scrolls along with the texture. As such it gives the impression while testing that the rotation gets faster over time, but this is only the result of the pivot being continuously offset more and more, messing up the math. \r\n\r\nAs a workaround, I've tried making the sprite itself the child of a position 2d node and rotate that instead, but for a reason I don't quite understand, the problem is still occurring. Next, I tried scrolling the texture with a shader instead, to see if that would produce different results. It did not. \r\n\r\nAfter posting on multiple help forums, I finally got a moderator on the godot Q&A forum to test out my project and see if he could fix it. His conclusion was that the problem was probably occurring due to an engine bug.\r\n\r\n**Here is a screenshot of the scene tree and the relevant script:**\r\n\r\nhttps://godotforums.org/uploads/editor/2b/z4afqzo940eo.png\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8281454/105940650-2282dc00-609f-11eb-9bcb-11db51052005.png)\r\n\r\nhttps://godotforums.org/uploads/editor/20/dzblywwu0zp8.png\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/8281454/105940656-257dcc80-609f-11eb-8e67-7b33cccd977d.png)\r\n\r\n\r\n**Steps to reproduce:**\r\n\r\n- Use a sprite, add a seamless texture imported with mirrored option enabled\r\n- Enable and configure the sprite's texture region according to the texture used\r\n- Through script, scroll the texture region on the y axis and have the scrolling move relative to texture rotation \r\n-  Through script, rotate the sprite\r\n\r\n**Original Project:**\r\n[Shmup_Project.zip](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/files/5877615/Shmup_Project.zip)\r\n\r\n**Sample Project**\r\n[Pivot Issue.zip](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/files/5884399/Pivot.Issue.zip)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n**Note:** Use Q and E keys to rotate while testing.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
