      "body": "### Godot version\n\nv4.0.dev.custom_build [bf322bacd]\n\n### System information\n\nmanjaro 21, AMD Radeon r7 200 series, Vulkan, 8GB Memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen you set the background mode to custom color, all metallic materials gets black:\r\n\r\nReality:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/58845030/137394023-1b960547-3d91-47ff-be00-04dbc46d1ab4.png)\r\n\r\nExpected:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/58845030/137394116-63fac236-4050-472e-9dd9-2fab21e7d92c.png)\r\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n* Create WorldEnviroment Node\r\n* Set Background mode to custom color\r\n* Place a model with material metallic at 1\r\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project\n\nN/a",
