      "body": "**Godot version:**\r\n3.2.1.stable.offical\r\n**OS/device including version:**\r\nwin 10 home 10.0.18362 build 18362\r\nHP laptop 15-da0xxx\r\n**Issue description:**\r\nWhen the autocomplete dialogue is clipped by the text editor region it doesn't add scrollbars.\r\n**Steps to reproduce:**\r\nopen the script editor and resize the window so it only shows 9 lines. type \"V\" it shows the complete autocomplete dialogue with scroll bar. type \"e\" so it's auto-completing \"Ve\" Vector2d is clipped off the top. \r\n![godot](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/25010423/81380473-98d64d00-90d0-11ea-85d1-b009d2d08289.png)\r\n\r\n**Minimal reproduction project:**\r\n\r\n[Map Editor.zip](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/files/4597514/Map.Editor.zip)\r\n",
